    "n1": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4756,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "N1 · Floating dock. Inbox, Tasks and Agents in one pill, with New task beside it. Only the current place shows its label. Second phone: tap Tasks again to open the switcher. The company name is its own menu (third phone), and your avatar in the corner opens You (fourth phone): profile, theme, push settings and a pointer to what lives on desktop. The dock hides while you scroll down and comes back on scroll up.",
      "fill": "purple"
    },
    "n2": {
      "x": 1900,
      "y": 4756,
      "w": 440,
      "text": "N2 · Tab bar. Five fixed tabs with labels, New task in the middle. Right: the You tab holds the company switcher, theme, and links to what lives on desktop. The most familiar pattern, but it takes about 80px all the time.",
      "fill": "blue"
    },
    "n5": {
      "x": 2900,
      "y": 4756,
      "w": 440,
      "text": "N5 · Now. A home screen instead of tabs: what needs you, agents at work, your projects. Right: every other screen sits one level down with a Now pill to come back. The calmest option, but moving between two places takes more taps.",
      "fill": "green"
    }
